Under the null, the static follows the F with these degrees of freedom. They must be nested and fitted to the same observations. So both these have to be true. So just because you have a nested model of, you know, the tree model, if you fit it on trees 1, 2, and 3 and fit another model on trees 4, 5, and 6, those are not nested models.

