0.05 is traditionally used, but you have to think of it as kind of a â€“ you should think of it as kind of evidence, right? So if I was running this and I had the ability to collect more data and I was right on the borderline like this, I would collect more data and see really as I collect more data, do I start to fall more on the â€“ does my P value tend to get smaller or tend to get larger?

